### 4. Pending Work
What's left unfinished or blocked?

### 5. Prompt Issues (rare)
Only if you notice the agent *consistently* misreading a whole class of task
because the system prompt itself is unclear or misleading — not a one-off slip —
flag it so the prompt can be improved. Emit a `<prompt_issue>` block naming the
offending template (e.g. `core_agent_system`). Skip this unless it's a real,
repeating pattern.

Keep it concise — this is a checkpoint, not a full summary.

### Output Format
Record learnings in XML blocks. Omit empty blocks.

- `<user_model>` — user model entries (each as `## Section Header`). Merged into `agent.md` (always in context).
- `<lesson topic="...">` — cross-session decisions, patterns, facts as bullets, grouped under a short kebab-case `topic`. Written to `memories/<topic>.md` and indexed (surfaced in context via the memory INDEX). Emit one block per topic.
- `<skill>` — at most one. Only if step 2 identified a genuinely reusable workflow.
- `<prompt_issue template="...">` — rare. Only per step 5, when a system-prompt template repeatedly misleads the agent. One short paragraph describing the misunderstanding.

